---
title: Easy Pork Ribs
servings: 6
cuisine: american
main_protein: pork
prep_time: "20 minutes"
cook_time: "80 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
  - pork
  - ribs
  - bbq
source: https://ontarioporkrecipes.ca/easy-pork-ribs
image: ../obsidian/attachments/easy-pork-ribs.jpg
leftover_portions: 2
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 325°F
  - Remove membrane from back ribs or trim fat from side ribs
  - Combine black pepper, red pepper flakes and thyme
  - Boil water for the baking sheets
---
For back ribs, preheat #oven{} to 325°F (160°C) and remove tough membrane on non-meaty side of @pork ribs{3%lb}. For side ribs, trim visible fat and preheat to 325°F (160°C).

Combine @black pepper{1%tbsp}, freshly ground, @red pepper flakes{1%tsp} and @dried thyme leaves{2%tsp} in a bowl. Season ribs, place meaty-side up on #baking sheets{}.

Add hot water to create approximately 1/4-inch depth. Cover with #foil{} and bake at 325°F until meat recedes from rib tips (about ~{1%hour} for back ribs, 2 hours for side ribs).

Remove ribs and discard liquid. Proceed to browning or refrigerate up to 3 days.

Oven method: Increase heat to 450°F (230°C). Brush @bbq sauce{1%cup} on one side, cook ~{5%minutes} until bubbly and golden. Flip, apply remaining sauce, cook 5 more minutes.

Grill method: Preheat #grill{} to high for 10 minutes, reduce to medium. Grill on medium-low heat for 15 minutes, brushing with sauce and turning occasionally.

-- Use Ontario side or back ribs; 1 to 2 cups of your favourite BBQ sauce.
